WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:01.805
ALEXIS MOUSSINE-POUCHKINE:
Where do you

00:00:01.805 --> 00:00:04.019
go to ask Google Cloud
Platform questions?

00:00:04.019 --> 00:00:05.700
How do you share best practices?

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:07.570
And how can you
learn from others?

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:10.170
How do you stay up
with the pace of GCP?

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:12.930
In this video, we'll walk
through some prominent

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:16.410
resources and also through
some less obvious ones that

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:18.660
may work well for you
in your GCP journey.

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:21.510
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:27.480
Having the right
resources of information

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:29.370
and using the right
communication channels

00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:32.580
can be the difference between a
regular and a highly productive

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:33.660
GCP user.

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:35.530
The good news is you
found this video,

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:37.210
so you're already
on the right path.

00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:39.990
It all starts with the
Google Cloud homepage

00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:42.330
at the cloud.google.com.

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:45.210
This page remains a reference
for product descriptions

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:46.680
and documentation.

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:49.740
Since many developers identify
themselves by the language

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:52.920
of their choice, we have landing
pages for the most popular

00:00:52.920 --> 00:01:02.460
languages supported by GCP, such
as Go, Python, Java, NoJS, PHP,

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:05.319
.NET, Ruby, and Kotlin.

00:01:05.319 --> 00:01:07.170
Let's take Go as an example.

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:09.360
The landing page
for Go will walk you

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:12.960
through how to deploy your
web apps using App Engine,

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:16.980
and how to use GCP's idiomatic
Go APIs and libraries.

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:18.930
If you look at
Kotlin, you'll find

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:22.770
quick starts for Compute Engine,
Kubernetes Engine, and App

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:25.620
Engine, as well as
code labs and tutorials

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:29.100
to build auto-scaling
backends for mobile apps,

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:31.920
and instructions for using
your favorite Java and Kotlin

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:33.300
frameworks.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:38.130
Blog posts are great resources
for both new and seasoned users

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:39.840
to stay on top of GCP.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:45.120
The main Google Cloud Blog at
cloud.google.com/blog typically

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:49.530
has multiple posts a day, and
covers products, features,

00:01:49.530 --> 00:01:51.870
and also partner and
customer stories.

00:01:51.870 --> 00:01:54.660
You are probably also interested
in content that is not

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:57.210
exclusively written by Google.

00:01:57.210 --> 00:01:59.520
The GCP Medium
publication is a list

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:02.160
of articles curated
by practitioners

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:04.110
for practitioners.

00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:06.630
If you'd like to share your
experience with the community,

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:09.150
this is a great
place to be noticed.

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:13.500
This publication also features
a weekly recap of the GCP news

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:15.510
in the last week.

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:18.270
And believe me, there's no
such thing as a quiet week.

00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:20.010
If you're into podcasts--

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:21.960
maybe you have a commute
or some other time

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:24.330
to listen to technical
audio content--

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:26.670
then you should
subscribe to at least one

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:28.710
of these two weekly podcasts--

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:33.120
the GCP podcast and
the Kubernetes podcast.

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:35.400
Both of them feature
news of the week

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:37.080
and interviews with
Google engineers,

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:41.370
as well as partners, customers,
and community members.

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:42.960
Since you're watching
this, you may

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:46.230
be interested in more video
content from the GCP YouTube

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:47.560
channel.

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:50.710
We have videos published
here on a regular basis,

00:02:50.710 --> 00:02:54.360
and most of them are grouped
into playlists around topics,

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:56.220
products, and events.

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:58.770
There are other several
related YouTube channels,

00:02:58.770 --> 00:03:04.170
such as Firebase, TensorFlow,
Google Developers, G Suite,

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:05.760
or Apigee.

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:07.530
If you're hanging
out on Twitter,

00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:10.290
you should definitely
follow Google Cloud Platform

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:13.800
@GCPCloud, and
consider also following

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:15.900
one of these active accounts--

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:20.130
Firebase, G Suite Developers,
Google Maps Platform,

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:23.130
Google Open Source,
and again, Apigee.

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:25.200
Several GCP members
monitor these

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:27.030
handles to engage
with the community,

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:30.090
and it can be a great way
to get the team's attention.

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:31.590
Of course, this is
not a replacement

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:33.150
to our support options.

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:35.100
While we're on the
topic of social media,

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:39.180
we also have spaces on Facebook
as well as on LinkedIn.

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:40.270
Check those out.

00:03:40.270 --> 00:03:44.580
The GCP community is large,
vibrant, and growing quickly.

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:48.440
It exists online and in a
variety of real-world places,

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:50.970
and this community
landing page covers both.

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:54.450
Community tutorials are
community-contributed how-tos

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:58.380
with an open publishing
process hosted on GitHub.

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:01.000
There are close to
200 tutorials to date.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:03.960
And if you cannot find what
you're looking for, you should

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:07.230
request it, or maybe even write
something yourself and submit

00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:08.490
it.

00:04:08.490 --> 00:04:12.360
On the real-world side,
user groups and GCP meet-ups

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:15.300
are great places where
like-minded people meet

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:18.870
to share their experiences,
their best practices, and maybe

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:20.730
even to find a job.

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:23.570
There are active meet-up
groups around the world,

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:25.530
and there should be one nearby.

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:27.510
If not, then create one.

00:04:27.510 --> 00:04:30.780
It's easy, and the personal
rewards are numerous.

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:32.820
You can also attend
conferences--

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:36.900
small, medium, or large ones,
such as the one organized

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:42.420
by Google, Google Cloud Next,
or our Summits or onboard events

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:44.490
in dozens of cities
around the world.

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:47.670
You will also find GCP content
in many industry events,

00:04:47.670 --> 00:04:51.600
such as OSCON, KubeCon,
Devoxx in Europe,

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:54.060
and of course, in
the more than 600

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:56.430
community-led DevFest events.

00:04:56.430 --> 00:04:58.920
In all these events, you
will be able to learn

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:02.310
from technical sessions,
meet with Cloud engineers,

00:05:02.310 --> 00:05:03.600
and ask questions.

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:07.350
Getting help from peers can
turn out to be a big asset,

00:05:07.350 --> 00:05:08.850
and some of it can
come in the form

00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:10.890
of answers on Stack Overflow.

00:05:10.890 --> 00:05:13.410
But did you know that
Google engineers maintain

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:16.710
and monitor a number
of GCP-related tags?

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:19.290
This is part of GCP
community support,

00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:21.690
and details are documented
in the page mentioned

00:05:21.690 --> 00:05:22.980
in the description below.

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:25.730
Of course, there's
always formal support.

00:05:25.730 --> 00:05:27.900
And if you're
starting out with GCP,

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:30.270
then I would suggest that
you purchase Silver Level

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:34.560
Support using a portion of
your $300 trial credit right

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:36.760
from the console in
the Support section.

00:05:36.760 --> 00:05:38.130
Here's a quick tip.

00:05:38.130 --> 00:05:40.440
With a picture being
worth a thousand words,

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:43.080
imagine the value to your
colleagues of a visual

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:46.320
representation of your
GCP architecture made with

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:52.500
great-looking icons and diagrams
from cloud.google.com/icons.

00:05:52.500 --> 00:05:56.010
This resource contains
vector graphics, PNGs,

00:05:56.010 --> 00:05:58.590
slides, and templates
for popular tools

00:05:58.590 --> 00:06:01.950
such as Lucidchart and Draw.io.

00:06:01.950 --> 00:06:04.260
And last but not least,
I couldn't leave you

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:07.240
without a cheat sheet,
the Google Cloud Four

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:09.090
Words or Less Cheat Sheet.

00:06:09.090 --> 00:06:11.820
The sheet comes in many
different formats, including

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:16.350
several print-friendly formats,
and it is maintained on GitHub.

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:18.840
It's a very popular resource,
and you should definitely

00:06:18.840 --> 00:06:20.010
check it out.

00:06:20.010 --> 00:06:23.370
As you can see, there are many
options for you to consider.

00:06:23.370 --> 00:06:25.700
Pick the ones that
work best for you,

00:06:25.700 --> 00:06:29.370
and share anything that you'll
find missing in the comments.

00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:32.800
If you like this video, please
like, subscribe, comment,

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:35.670
share, and look forward to
more GCP Essentials videos.

00:06:35.670 --> 00:06:38.720
[MUSIC PLAYING]

